From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craig Johnson <1545411+captainpacket@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:44:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mgmt-static: raise the seeded 0.0.0.0/0 route's distance to
 250

MEASURED live on example-lab-shared (2026-09-19, task 210829): siteC-dc-leaf01
correctly originates a static default toward the DC firewall and
redistributes it into BGP (bgp.import: {static: {}}). siteC-dc-spine01's own
BGP table shows that route received, valid, and best-path from leaf01. But
spine01's RIB (`show ip route 0.0.0.0/0`) still shows `S 0.0.0.0/0 directly
connected, Management0` as gateway of last resort -- the BGP-best route
never installs, because the mgmt-runtime-seeded static (0007) carries the
default administrative distance for a static route (1), which always beats
a protocol-learned default (eBGP 20, OSPF 110) for the identical prefix.
Confirmed via `show running-config section ip route`: `ip route 0.0.0.0/0
Management0`, no distance argument. Same on siteC-dc-leaf02/03/04 and
spine02. Only siteC-dc-leaf01 has a working default route, and only because
it happens to carry its OWN competing local static at the same prefix --
not because the mechanism is correct, but by coincidence of collision.
Live impact: three of four DC-fabric hosts (behind leaf02/03/04) have no
Internet reachability; only the host behind leaf01 does.

This is not a new failure mode invented by this fix -- it's the exact
shape 0008's readiness gate already has a proven-correct fallback for.
0008's SKYFORGE_MGMT_RETURN_CIDRS-anchored clause (`proto gated`, no via)
is what already lets siteC-dc-leaf01 go Ready today, precisely because its
own local static displaced the mgmt default. Raising the seeded static's
distance to 250 (worse than any protocol AD, still better than no route)
makes every OTHER cEOS node take that SAME already-proven fallback path
whenever the lab's own design gives it a protocol default, instead of
only the node whose local config happens to collide with the seeded
prefix. A node with no protocol default at all is unaffected: the seeded
static remains the only default present and is still installed.

Considered and rejected: scoping the seeded route to
SKYFORGE_MGMT_RETURN_CIDRS only (dropping the blanket 0.0.0.0/0 line
entirely). patches/netlab/09-kne-config-lanes-and-quirks.patch:1229-1241
records a related VRF/prefix-separation attempt that broke a different
(MLAG host-role) bring-up case measured 2026-09-12 -- prefix/VRF
separation for this exact mechanism has prior-attempt risk. Distance is
the narrower lever: it changes nothing about which routes exist, only
which one wins when both are present.


---
 controllers/ceoslabdevice_controller.go       | 21 ++++++++++++++++++-
 .../ceoslabdevice_controller_unit_test.go     | 11 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/controllers/ceoslabdevice_controller.go b/controllers/ceoslabdevice_controller.go
index 466753d..fa2a716 100644
--- a/controllers/ceoslabdevice_controller.go
+++ b/controllers/ceoslabdevice_controller.go
@@ -1745,6 +1745,25 @@ func mgmtRuntimeConfigEnabled(device *ceoslabv1alpha1.CEosLabDevice, envVarsMap
 //     an earlier one on replay. The block is appended LAST so EOS installing the
 //     address/routes also witnesses that the entire seeded config replayed.
 //
+//     The 0.0.0.0/0 line carries an explicit distance (default 250, override
+//     via SKYFORGE_MGMT_DEFAULT_DISTANCE), NOT the static default of 1.
+//     MEASURED live on example-lab-shared (2026-09-19): a cEOS fabric node whose
+//     lab design originates and correctly BGP-redistributes its own default
+//     route (proven received and best-path on a downstream node's BGP table)
+//     never had it installed in the RIB, because this mgmt static — AD 1 —
+//     always wins the same 0.0.0.0/0 slot over a protocol-learned default
+//     (eBGP AD 20, OSPF 110). Only a node with its OWN competing local static
+//     happened to work, purely by coincidence of prefix collision. Distance
+//     250 makes a protocol default win whenever the lab actually has one,
+//     while this line remains the last-resort default (still installed, still
+//     read by the readiness gate below) on any node with no protocol default
+//     at all. The readiness gate's SKYFORGE_MGMT_RETURN_CIDRS-anchored
+//     fallback clause already exists to certify management reachability on
+//     exactly this "protocol default displaced the mgmt default" shape (see
+//     the sibling readiness-gate script) — this change makes every routed
+//     cEOS node take that same already-proven path, not just the ones that
+//     happen to carry a locally-conflicting static.
+//
 // Address prefix length (canary br1, cEOS 4.34.2f, 2026-07-18): EOS REJECTS a
 // /32 interface address ("% Prefix length must be less than 32") — and a
 // rejected line would abort config replay. The prefix is therefore derived at
@@ -1817,7 +1836,7 @@ if [ -n "${SKYFORGE_MGMT_EOS_INTF:-}" ]; then
       printf 'interface %s\n' "${SKYFORGE_MGMT_EOS_INTF}"
       if [ -n "${mtu}" ]; then printf '   mtu %s\n' "${mtu}"; fi
       printf '   ip address %s/%s\n' "${ip}" "${pfx}"
-      printf 'ip route 0.0.0.0/0 %s\n' "${SKYFORGE_MGMT_EOS_INTF}"
+      printf 'ip route 0.0.0.0/0 %s %s\n' "${SKYFORGE_MGMT_EOS_INTF}" "${SKYFORGE_MGMT_DEFAULT_DISTANCE:-250}"
       _oldifs="${IFS}"
       IFS=','
       for cidr in ${SKYFORGE_MGMT_RETURN_CIDRS:-}; do
diff --git a/controllers/ceoslabdevice_controller_unit_test.go b/controllers/ceoslabdevice_controller_unit_test.go
index eafacd5..5a941f7 100644
--- a/controllers/ceoslabdevice_controller_unit_test.go
+++ b/controllers/ceoslabdevice_controller_unit_test.go
@@ -319,6 +319,10 @@ func TestGetPodSeedInitMaterializesMgmtRuntime(t *testing.T) {
 		"if [ \"${cidr}\" = \"${addr_cidr}\" ]; then continue; fi",
 		// interface-form routes: no gateway to embed, EOS ARPs per destination
 		"ip route 0.0.0.0/0 %s",
+		// distance 250, not the static default of 1 -- see the startupSeedScript
+		// doc comment (2026-09-19 fix): an AD-1 mgmt default always wins the RIB
+		// over a protocol-learned default on the same prefix.
+		"SKYFORGE_MGMT_DEFAULT_DISTANCE:-250",
 		// observed-MTU materialization (runtime truth, like the IP)
 		"/sys/class/net/eth0/mtu",
 	} {
@@ -378,7 +382,12 @@ func TestStartupSeedScriptCIDRMath(t *testing.T) {
 	for _, want := range []string{
 		"hostname leaf1\n",
 		"   ip address 198.18.0.132/15\n",
-		"ip route 0.0.0.0/0 Management0\n",
+		// Distance 250, not the static default of 1: MEASURED live on
+		// example-lab-shared (2026-09-19) that an AD-1 mgmt default always wins
+		// the RIB over a protocol-learned default on the same prefix, even
+		// when the protocol route is correctly received and best-path in
+		// BGP -- see the doc comment on startupSeedScript above.
+		"ip route 0.0.0.0/0 Management0 250\n",
 		"ip route 100.64.0.0/10 Management0\n",
 	} {
 		if !strings.Contains(got, want) {
